{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh","id":1547646,"title":"The End is Nigh","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-09T10:36:32-08:00","id":1547646,"title":"The End is Nigh","content":"The Advanced PDFs of what will probably be the last two official books of the M20 line have been released. Faces of Magick was released earlier this week; and from what I hear, it's a big book of NPCs. Forbidden and Forgotten Orders was just released, and is to the Disparate Alliance as Lore of the Traditions is to the Traditions. The only faction that M20 never got around to are the Marauders. <br /> <br /> Final release to the general public is still a future date; but it's closing in quickly. After that, the only new material will be whatever shows up on STV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-09T15:23:12-08:00","id":1547650,"title":"","content":"I wish we could get a few more books. Especially as we are willing to pay up front in kickstarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-10T13:16:22-08:00","id":1547667,"title":"","content":"Thinking of Marauder factions just made me consider a conspiracy of Avatars who, on the occasions they go Marauder, continue some kind of grand plan. They don't actually drive their mages towards Marauderdom so only one or two of them is truly active at any given point in history. Instead they mostly plan and leave messages for each other through hidden symbols, Promethean-style.<br /> <br /> Of course it runs aground in that Avatars don't really control Marauders, so there would need to be something more for this to be workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T02:55:18-08:00","id":1547692,"title":"","content":"Anyone else deeply wishing Paradox doesn't start making M5 after this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T06:31:17-08:00","id":1547693,"title":"","content":"I would like to see some more Mage stuff. My reaction to the WoD5 so far has been mixed, but I would give M5 a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T06:55:20-08:00","id":1547694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547693#post1547693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see some more Mage stuff. My reaction to the WoD5 so far has been mixed, but I would give M5 a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, the fifth edition stuff seems to reject imagination, fun, and creativity. &quot;Lay down in the gutter and die.&quot; can, and has, worked in many art forms, but can it work in an RPG? I don't say it's impossible, but I've seen no examples of that that actually worked as a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T13:22:22-08:00","id":1547699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547694#post1547694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thematically, the fifth edition stuff seems to reject imagination, fun, and creativity. &quot;Lay down in the gutter and die.&quot; can, and has, worked in many art forms, but can it work in an RPG? I don't say it's impossible, but I've seen no examples of that that actually worked as a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's especially antithetical to Mage: The Ascension as a game. The entire ethos of Mage is telling people &quot;YOU have the power to change the world, for good or ill&quot;.<br /> <br /> If W5 is anything to go by, M5 would triple down on the worst &quot;Reality is calcified, there's nothing you can do&quot; of Revised edition, with none of the quick shift that edition did partway through to salvage player relations.<br /> <br /> I've seen nothing from WoD5 that makes me want to see what Paradox will do to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T07:36:46-08:00","id":1547739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547693#post1547693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see some more Mage stuff. My reaction to the WoD5 so far has been mixed, but I would give M5 a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Onyx Path were writing it, I'd buy it in a heartbeat. As things stand, I intend a &quot;try before you buy&quot; route when and if it comes out. <br /> <br /> I do fear that they intend to turn M5 into another &quot;sucks to be you&quot; game; the folks on charge of Paradox's World of Darkness IP seem to have a very specific idea of what the World of Darkness ought to be; and they apparently <i>do </i>believe that if you don't play the game that way, you're playing it wrong. And I'm worried that they'll take the nuanced glorious mess that <b>Mage</b> currently is and will attempt to dumb it down. <br /> <br /> With that said, I prefer to be optimistic when I can be; and in that vein, I think that one thing that they have a track record of doing (borrowing heavily from Chronicles of Darkness) could actually work out for the better where M5's Magick is concerned. Namely, and I say this with utmost love, M20's Magick system is an unwieldy mess; and you could do far worse that to just rip it out and start over with Awakening's magic system as a starting point. <br /> <br /> Emphasis on &quot;starting point&quot;: the single biggest difference between Ascension and Awakening is that Ascension has individual Paradigm and Practice; Awakening at best deemphasizes that, and tends to outright ignore it. <br /> <br /> So in an &quot;M5 done right&quot;, I'd want something to the effect of M20's Focus rules not only integrated into the Magick system, but given a place of prominence in the game: rather than putting it in the back of the book almost as an afterthought, put it front and center in the character creation process, and reference it in the &quot;how to work an Effect&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-15T07:23:39-08:00","id":1547757,"title":"","content":"It's definitely possible to rewrite the game mechanics of sphere magic without in any way touching the in universe place and metaphysics of sphere magic. In fact, it is technically easier to do so than doing both. I say technically, because though it is easier to do, it isn't necessarily easier to see that you can do that. It's an unfortunately common pitfall, in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T05:59:21-08:00","id":1547847,"title":"","content":"Maybe the World of Darkness needs to split. I've often described the Cainite Vampires, the Garou, and the Wraiths, as the Damned, the Doomed, and the Lost. Quick succinct descriptions of their situations. But the Mages and the Changelings are different. Maybe we need to drop a unified WoD as an idea. M:tA and C:tD could have one metaplot/metaverse and V:tM, W:tA, and W:tO could have another. <br /> <br /> Other games like H:tR, mummy, demon, and Kindred of the East can be fit in where they fit best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T22:12:18-08:00","id":1547886,"title":"","content":"W5 is weird because it feels more like the common gripes of people who didnt like wta or prefered 'street' vtm applied uncritically. H5 is even weirder because its a generic urban monster hunter game in a market full of them and is ultimatly pointless<br /> with that in mind i cant really see what they could really contribute to mage of note. They'd resent the raw utility of mage magic and struggle with the larger than life aspects or morally dubious aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T15:16:41-08:00","id":1547900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547886#post1547886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 is weird because it feels more like the common gripes of people who didnt like wta or prefered 'street' vtm applied uncritically. H5 is even weirder because its a generic urban monster hunter game in a market full of them and is ultimatly pointless<br /> with that in mind i cant really see what they could really contribute to mage of note. They'd resent the raw utility of mage magic and struggle with the larger than life aspects or morally dubious aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also imagine Paradox's designers would get fixated on the idea of centering the moral highground wholly on the Technocracy, with the logic that they NEED to make the proponents of science the protagonists against the forces of mysticism and fringe beliefs because they're RIGHT.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, they are. Let it never be said the Traditions don't have a different subtext in our current political climate of conspiracism and skepticism of modern science.<br /> <br /> But that's not really how Mage: The Ascension was conceived or developed. Nor does it take into account its larger Punk themes or sensibilities. I think Paradox's writers, given their track record, may flatten the Ascension War (assuming they don't jettison it entirely, engine of conflict generation be damned) and make all the factions both less interesting and more Flanderized. While doing so in a way to uncritically reinforce a Neo-Lib centrist understanding of belief and politics. When the whole point of MtAs was to sincerely examine belief systems, especially within the framework of the power structures they exist within and prop up.<br /> <br /> I see the Paradox writers thinking, &quot;Well, obviously the Technocracy are just correct, so why would we want to make anyone else playable?&quot;<br /> <br /> (A fear of mine furthered by the complete unwillingness to engage with the delicate subjects of Indigenous cultures and history in W5. If they're willing to file off cultural signifiers for factions in Werewolf, and in the process make all the tribes culturally White in practice, what will they do to the Chakravanti, Akashayana, Cult of Ecstasy, or especially <i>Dreamspeakers</i>?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T08:47:16-08:00","id":1547909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547886#post1547886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 is weird because it feels more like the common gripes of people who didnt like wta or prefered 'street' vtm applied uncritically. H5 is even weirder because its a generic urban monster hunter game in a market full of them and is ultimatly pointless<br /> with that in mind i cant really see what they could really contribute to mage of note. They'd resent the raw utility of mage magic and struggle with the larger than life aspects or morally dubious aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well given that, I think the consensus will certainly be on the chopping block. Indeed, I suspect that it will be removed in a way that makes the Ascension War incoherent. Like making awakened magic some unreal thing that only temporarily suspends &quot;true reality&quot; and making the Technocracy not use awakened magic at all but instead purely exploit the rules of said &quot;true reality.&quot; (But still use the mechanics for sphere magic anyways, just to be extra confusing). <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't be surprised if they inflicted some kind of metaphysical change on the world that forced the standard setting to be one of street level play with little to no access to otherworlds. Possibly some kind of large, supernatural natural disaster that blocked off the umbra, but just for mages since W5 has already been written. Some kind of avatar related storm, perhaps?<br /> <br /> Yeah, for those more familiar than I am with Paradox, what are the odds they are aware of how badly that aspect of Mage Revised went over? And if they are, what are the odds they care?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T12:02:26-08:00","id":1547915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547909#post1547909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well given that, I think the consensus will certainly be on the chopping block. Indeed, I suspect that it will be removed in a way that makes the Ascension War incoherent. Like making awakened magic some unreal thing that only temporarily suspends &quot;true reality&quot; and making the Technocracy not use awakened magic at all but instead purely exploit the rules of said &quot;true reality.&quot; (But still use the mechanics for sphere magic anyways, just to be extra confusing).</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has pushed for years for alternate takes on the Consensus that makes it possible to view the Technocracy as actually having a point and not automatically being &quot;all liars or dupes&quot;\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026I hope they don't do what you're speculating. I don't want the role reversal of the <i>Technocracy</i> being objectively right and the <i>Traditions</i> being liars and dupes; I don't want the metaphysics to be &quot;flattened&quot;. I <i>want</i> fans of the Traditions to be able to say that they're on to something, <i>\u200b\u200b\u200btoo</i>. I wouldn't mind in the least opening the <i>\u200b\u200b\u200bpossibility</i> that the Technocracy is doing something fundamentally different from the Traditions; but that shouldn't be objectively right any more than the Traditions' collective metaphysics should be. <br /> <br /> I don't want Mage's metaphysics to be dumbed down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T12:28:19-08:00","id":1547916,"title":"","content":"But getting back to the original subject: are there any books that you would have liked to have seen in the. M20 line that they never got around to publishing? For me, it would be a Book of Quiet. something having to do with the state of Quiet, and the Marauders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T15:04:57-08:00","id":1547920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547909#post1547909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, for those more familiar than I am with Paradox, what are the odds they are aware of how badly that aspect of Mage Revised went over? And if they are, what are the odds they care?</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect, in the latter case, very low odds. Paradox were willing to throw the entire existing fanbase for both Werewolf: The Apocalypse AND Hunter: The Reckoning under the bus, simply to chase potential new players. Complete ignoring that the best brand ambassadors for a new edition are fans of the old work, tirelessly on-boarding new people with their enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> There's a distinct possibility, no matter how remote or senseless, that making new editions of the World of Darkness games is, in the end, an IP gesture. That they don't particularly care how successful the books are, so long as it can be a jumping off point for tie-in products in other mediums.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T17:00:34-08:00","id":1547923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547920#post1547920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a distinct possibility, no matter how remote or senseless, that making new editions of the World of Darkness games is, in the end, an IP gesture. That they don't particularly care how successful the books are, so long as it can be a jumping off point for tie-in products in other mediums.</div> </div> </div> </div>What tie in products? Like is it bloodlines 2? Which paradox is starting to have doubts if this article is accurate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/pa...-someone-else/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/pa...-someone-else/</a> - It's been nearly a decade since Paradox Interactive acquired White Wolf and the World of Darkness, and nearly as long since it started working with Hard Suit Labs based on its pitch for Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines 2. And boy has it been a rough time. <br /> After four years working in secret, Hard Suit and Paradox announced Bloodlines 2 in 2019. We'd be playing it in 2020, the pair said. Then it was delayed. And delayed again. The 2020 target became 2021, and then it was delayed indefinitely, with Hard Suit given the boot.<br /> <br /> For a while, it seemed like cancellation was inevitable. And it did almost end up in the bin. &quot;If we hadn't found The Chinese Room,&quot; deputy CEO Mattias Lilja tells me, &quot;and seen what they'd done with the early work, [cancellation] would have been the next logical step, because we could not continue as we did.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lilja believes it's in a better place now\u2014though it was recently struck with yet another delay, pushing it out of 2024 and into the first half of 2025. &quot;It's been in development a very long time, but we are starting to see the game shape up to be something we can\u2026 we think it will be a World of Darkness experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's strangely tepid praise, but also refreshing. The reason for this interview was not the usual marketing-driven fare. No big announcements. No hype. Just a rather frank explanation about what's going on at Paradox, the reasons why it's been struggling recently, and what it's doing to change its fortunes. But even with that in mind, there seems to be a bit of nervousness about how Bloodlines 2 will ultimately be received. And it's not something that Paradox wants to go through again.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is not in our strategic direction to make this kind of game,&quot; Lilja says. &quot;So if Bloodlines 2, God willing, is successful, Bloodlines 3 [will be] done by someone else, on the license from us. I would say it's the sort of strategic way this would work. So it's still an outlier from what we're supposed to do, we don't know that stuff, so we should probably let other people do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the future of Bloodlines 2, specifically: &quot;We don't drop games. We make sure they work. We make sure they fulfil the promise that they have. The rest is very much up to the players.&quot; So you can expect the usual slate of updates and fixes, but DLC? I wouldn't hold your breath.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think some studios do strategic investments, long term things, because they feel that the cost of not doing it is too high. But, I mean, I think it's fairly clear, at least to me, and I think to you, even in the best of cases, Bloodlines does not have a super long shelf life. That's not the way these games behave. You have an influx of players, there's a bit of word of mouth, and they have a high peak, and then they trail off. And it's not the type of gameplay that develops over time that much. So I think that's part of why these types of games are not really that attractive to us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yet it was the persistence of Bloodlines' fans that inspired this sequel, 20 years after the original. Better supported RPGs, meanwhile, can keep going year after year, as evidenced by the incredibly long life of Bethesda RPGs. And then there's Baldur's Gate\u2014a 26-year-old series that's just spawned its third game, which in turn has been one of Steam's most played games for over a year, despite the lack of DLC. Some RPGs have an incredibly long tail. But it is clear they aren't in Paradox's wheelhouse, and passing the licence to other caretakers might be the smart call here. </div> </div> </div><br /> Like there's the cyoas but let's be honest cyoa's are really niche genre that's facing stiff compation from Japanese LN's so I dubout they're part of any multimedia push.<br /> <br /> Like Honstly from the looks of thing wod5 is in a holding position where Renegade churns out all the core books before Paradox promptly put the IP on ice to maybe sell it in the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T06:23:00-08:00","id":1547930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547646-the-end-is-nigh?p=1547916#post1547916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But getting back to the original subject: are there any books that you would have liked to have seen in the. M20 line that they never got around to publishing? For me, it would be a Book of Quiet. something having to do with the state of Quiet, and the Marauders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know metaplot is a dirty word around here but I would have loved a &quot;Beckett's Jyhad Diary&quot; style look into <i>possible</i> metaplot advancements in the preceding years. I know this is touched on lightly in the M20 big book (what isnt?!) but I'm talking about a real deep dive. Now, the structure of BJD was largely constructed around chapters based on updating the various &quot;by night&quot; and &quot;region&quot; books and Mage has significantly fewer of those. So we'd probably focus on updating chantries and constructs explored in various Trad/Conv books as well as the Book of Chantries.<br /> <br /> There would have to be a major editorial decision regarding the Avatar Storm and the accessibility of Horizon Realms. Although I'm lukewarm on AS I do think the book would benefit from a strong focus on earthside locations. My personal preference would be to have access to/from Horizon realms temporarily disrupted and only recently reinstated. There's lots of plot hooks in there, including a sort of Awakened class conflict that has fascinated me recently.<br /> <br /> Briefly, I've been thinking about how Nodes, Tass, and Chantries receded from importance in First Edition. I've settled on as the kind of &quot;secret history&quot; of the Ascension War. <b>&quot;After WW2 there both the Traditions and Technocracy became overfocused on Horizon Realms. To power these realms both organizations prioritized securing and holding powerful nodes. This left a shortage of tass/quintessence available for earthside endeavors and inefficient expenditures of resources to secure new or newly available nodes.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> This sets It sets up a &quot;haves vs have nots&quot; conflict regarding inequality within both organizations. Why is the most powerful node in New Jersey (Edison's workshop) sending it quintessence to Horizon while you're out here busting your butt in New Jersey fighting a losing action against the Technocracy to save your 1 point urban garden node? Why are you literally slinging street drugs to gangbangers while your Progenitor Research Director is perfecting his cat-girl sex slaves in Research Plantation No. 4?The disruption and re-establishment of contact allows these conflicts erupt.<br /> <br /> If the quintessese from the nodes you control isn't going to the Cat Girl Plantation than maybe you don't have to sling street drugs to fund your next research project. Maybe you can actually accomplish something worthwhile and that'll all be destroyed if your supervisor (who was halfway to Nephandus before they lost contact anyways) reasserts authority. Maybe since Dossitep went kablooey the Verbena have been able to assert primacy over the Stonehenge node and that has the Hermetics feeling some kinda way? Someone finally gets around to clensing the Dachau node that Vormass used and discovers exactly how many Tradition Masters made use of the assassination services of the Consanguinity of Eternal Joy and how that enabled them hide their corruption for so long?<br /> <br /> So, I want both an incremental update and a total upsetting of the table. A worldwide phenomenon with local consequences (and we know how well that went over last time). I know that's a hard sell to most mage fans but disagreeing about the basic concepts of Mage is one of the oldest traditions in the Mage fandom so lets not stop now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}